# Generated data (always reproducible from generators)
candidates/*/environment/workspace/data/
candidates/*/environment/workspace/warehouse/
tools/task0*/.ws
tools/task0*/.oracle
tools/task0*/.world
tools/set_gemini_key.sh
submission/
submission.zip
logs/final-*.log
logs/tb3-check-*.log
logs/run_*.out

# `/jobs/` above has been ignored since the project began, so no Harbor job artefact has ever been
# tracked. For the nine phase-3 prospective trials that is deliberately overridden with `git add -f`,
# because the trajectories are the primary evidence for the frozen trajectory analysis and belong in
# version control. The only thing still excluded is the collected copy of each task's read-only input
# database: it is byte-reproducible from the frozen generator, it is 250 MB across the nine trials, and
# its digest is verified against the frozen extract digest for every trial in
# research/phase3/exposure/collected_db_digests.txt.
jobs/*-prospective-*/**/artifacts/workspace/data/*.sqlite

# ---- publication exclusions (added when the project was published) ----
# Raw Harbor job trees for the Gemini arm total ~1.8 GB. A curated subset is tracked;
# the rest is reproducible by re-running the task with `harbor run`.
# submission_final10.zip is 131 MB, above GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit.
submission_final10.zip
submission.zip
submission_5task_fallback.zip
research_review.zip
/submission/
*.bundle
/submission_final10/
